This project builds on the following works.

1. SegMoTE
   Yujie Lu, Jingwen Li, Sibo Ju, Yanzhou Su, He Yao, Yisong Liu, Min Zhu and
   Junlong Cheng. "SegMoTE: Token-Level Mixture of Experts for Medical Image
   Segmentation." IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition
   (CVPR), 2026. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.19213
   Source: https://github.com/InMyDreammer/SegMoTE
   Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 InMyDreammer

   The SegMoTE sources are not redistributed in this repository. They are fetched
   at a pinned commit by setup_upstream.py. The model graph, the mask decoder and
   the released weights are the work of the SegMoTE authors. The contribution here
   is the compression method, the evaluation protocol and the analysis built on
   top of that model.

2. Segment Anything Model
   Alexander Kirillov et al. "Segment Anything." IEEE/CVF International Conference
   on Computer Vision (ICCV), 2023. https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCV51070.2023.00371
   Source: https://github.com/facebookresearch/segment-anything
   Licence: Apache License 2.0

   Portions of the SegMoTE model code derive from the Segment Anything Model.

3. ISIC 2016 lesion segmentation data
   David Gutman et al., 2016. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1605.01397
   Hosted by the International Skin Imaging Collaboration. The data are
   downloaded from the challenge host by the user and are not redistributed
   here; their terms of use are set by the ISIC archive. For illustration only,
   assets/qualitative_cases.png shows ISIC 2016 test images 0009083, 0010378,
   0000138, 0009882, 0000222, 0011152 and 0008992, and assets/architecture.png
   shows a dermoscopic input thumbnail.
